<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ipiq-Adad II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 19th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ipiq-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadad">Adad</a> II was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> in the Diyala region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in the 19th century BCE. He expanded the power of Eshnunna by conquest, extending its reach along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> and towards the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. His sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadusha">Dadusha</a> continued his expansion, making Eshnunna a leading Mesopotamian power.</p></div>
